Subject: [PATCH 11/11] UI: trace the update half of a frame

Round 20 narrowed the port's remaining failure to a nine-call window and could
not narrow it further, because none of those calls says anything.

The trace from patch 0010 shows the emu thread completing exactly two frames —
both submitted, both presented, both fences returned — and then never beginning
a third. `PUSH: BeginFrame` comes from `g_draw->BeginFrame()` at the top of the
render half, and it is the first thing in a frame that leaves any trace of its
own. So a thread that stops anywhere above that line stops invisibly: everything
before it is bookkeeping that logs nothing on a quiet frame.

This names the call about to be entered, for each of them. It is deliberately
dumb — no timing, no nesting, just which one was last announced — because the
question is only "which of these did not return".

Compiled to nothing unless PPSSPP_FRAME_TRACE is defined, and the hunk in
UI/CMakeLists.txt scopes that define to this one file, so switching it on costs
a single object rather than the whole ccache. Same shape as the OpenGL trace in
patch 0010, and for the same reason.

diff --git a/UI/CMakeLists.txt b/UI/CMakeLists.txt
index 6ad1a9ac5..af05cb3b8 100644
--- a/UI/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/UI/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -123,3 +123,11 @@ list(APPEND UISource
 add_library(ppsspp_ui STATIC ${UISource})
 target_link_libraries(ppsspp_ui Common Core)
 setup_target_project(ppsspp_ui UI)
+
+# The per-frame update trace, off unless a round asks for it. Scoped to the one file
+# with the markers in it, for the same reason the OpenGL trace is scoped in
+# Common/CMakeLists.txt: an instrument that costs a full rebuild is one nobody turns on.
+if(PPSSPP_FRAME_TRACE)
+	set_source_files_properties(NativeApp.cpp PROPERTIES COMPILE_DEFINITIONS PPSSPP_FRAME_TRACE)
+	message(STATUS "NativeFrame update trace enabled (PPSSPP_FRAME_TRACE)")
+endif()
diff --git a/UI/NativeApp.cpp b/UI/NativeApp.cpp
index d715605c2..a449f8e35 100644
--- a/UI/NativeApp.cpp
+++ b/UI/NativeApp.cpp
@@ -1103,7 +1103,21 @@ void CallbackPostRender(UIContext *dc, void *userdata) {
 
 static void SendMouseDeltaAxis();
 
+// A frame's update half, step by step, for a platform where a thread can stop without
+// saying so. Every call below runs before g_draw->BeginFrame(), which is the first thing
+// in a frame that leaves any trace of its own — so a thread that stops in this stretch
+// stops invisibly, and the only way to name the call it stopped in is to say which one
+// is about to be entered.
+//
+// Compiled to nothing unless a build asks for it.
+#ifdef PPSSPP_FRAME_TRACE
+#define FRAME_TRACE(step) INFO_LOG(Log::System, "NativeFrame: %s", step)
+#else
+#define FRAME_TRACE(step) (void)0
+#endif
+
 void NativeFrame(GraphicsContext *graphicsContext) {
+	FRAME_TRACE("enter");
 	PROFILE_END_FRAME();
 
 	if (!(Core_IsActive() || Core_IsStepping()))
@@ -1123,28 +1137,36 @@ void NativeFrame(GraphicsContext *graphicsContext) {
 	ProcessWheelRelease(NKCODE_EXT_MOUSEWHEEL_DOWN, startTime, false);
 
 	// it's ok to call this redundantly with DoFrame from EmuScreen
+	FRAME_TRACE("Achievements::Idle");
 	Achievements::Idle();
 
+	FRAME_TRACE("g_DownloadManager.Update");
 	g_DownloadManager.Update();
 
+	FRAME_TRACE("g_Discord.Update");
 	g_Discord.Update();
 
+	FRAME_TRACE("g_OSD.Update");
 	g_OSD.Update();
 
 	_dbg_assert_(graphicsContext != nullptr);
 	_dbg_assert_(g_screenManager != nullptr);
 
+	FRAME_TRACE("g_GameManager.Update");
 	g_GameManager.Update();
 
 	if (GetUIState() != UISTATE_INGAME) {
+		FRAME_TRACE("g_BackgroundAudio.Update");
 		// Note: We do this from NativeFrame so that the graphics context is
 		// guaranteed valid, to be safe - g_gameInfoCache messes around with textures.
 		g_BackgroundAudio.Update();
 	}
 
+	FRAME_TRACE("g_iconCache.FrameUpdate");
 	g_iconCache.FrameUpdate();
 
 	if (g_audioBackend) {
+		FRAME_TRACE("g_audioBackend->FrameUpdate");
 		g_audioBackend->FrameUpdate(g_Config.bAutoSwitchAudioDevice);
 	}
 
@@ -1154,8 +1176,10 @@ void NativeFrame(GraphicsContext *graphicsContext) {
 		debugFlags |= Draw::DebugFlags::PROFILE_TIMESTAMPS;
 	if (g_Config.bGpuLogProfiler)
 		debugFlags |= Draw::DebugFlags::PROFILE_SCOPES;
+	FRAME_TRACE("g_draw->BeginFrame");
 	g_draw->BeginFrame(debugFlags);
 
+	FRAME_TRACE("ProcessScreenSwitches");
 	g_screenManager->ProcessScreenSwitches();
 
 	// Process queued events.
